Initial Package Version: 2.28.1
BFSOS refresh: 2026-09-10 for Requests 2.34.2
Upstream Status: downstream distribution policy
Origin: Linux From Scratch / Fedora / Arch-derived policy, refreshed for BFSOS
Description: Prefer the BFSOS system CA bundle and drop the certifi runtime dependency.

Requests explicitly permits distribution packagers to replace certs.where().
BFSOS uses /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt, maintained by ca-certificates + make-ca.
The _PIP_STANDALONE_CERT override is retained for pip's standalone bootstrap path.

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -18,8 +18,7 @@ requires-python = ">=3.10"
 dependencies = [
     "charset_normalizer>=2,<4",
     "idna>=2.5,<4",
-    "urllib3>=1.26,<3",
-    "certifi>=2023.5.7"
+    "urllib3>=1.26,<3"
 ]
 dynamic = ["version"]
 
diff --git a/src/requests/certs.py b/src/requests/certs.py
--- a/src/requests/certs.py
+++ b/src/requests/certs.py
@@ -12,7 +12,14 @@ environment, you can change the definition of where() to return a separately
 packaged CA bundle.
 """
 
-from certifi import where
+import os
+
+if "_PIP_STANDALONE_CERT" not in os.environ:
+    def where():
+        return "/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt"
+else:
+    def where():
+        return os.environ["_PIP_STANDALONE_CERT"]
 
 if __name__ == "__main__":
     print(where())
